STATEMENT 2: GetProductByIdAsync
================================================================================
Original MS SQL Statement:
WITH ProductHistory AS (
    SELECT 
        ProductId,
        LAG(Price) OVER (ORDER BY ModifiedDate) as PreviousPrice,
        LAG(StockQuantity) OVER (ORDER BY ModifiedDate) as PreviousStock
    FROM Products
    WHERE ProductId = @ProductId
)
SELECT 
    p.ProductId,
    p.Name,
    p.Description,
    p.Price,
    p.StockQuantity,
    p.CreatedDate,
    p.ModifiedDate,
    ph.PreviousPrice,
    ph.PreviousStock,
    CASE 
        WHEN ph.PreviousPrice IS NOT NULL THEN 
            ROUND(((p.Price - ph.PreviousPrice) / ph.PreviousPrice) * 100, 2)
        ELSE NULL
    END as PriceChangePercentage
FROM Products p
LEFT JOIN ProductHistory ph ON p.ProductId = ph.ProductId
WHERE p.ProductId = @ProductId

DMS Tool Output:
{
  "conversion_timestamp": "2026-02-06T22:57:27.155828",
  "status": "error",
  "error": "Metadata model creation failed: {'error': 'Unknown metadata model creation status: RECEIVED'}",
  "error_timestamp": "2026-02-06T22:57:31.269638"
}

Manual Conversion Applied:
- CTEs are compatible with PostgreSQL
- LAG window function is compatible with PostgreSQL
- Parameter @ProductId will be handled by Npgsql (uses $1 internally)
- Result: No syntax changes needed - statement is PostgreSQL compatible as-is

